    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7b7dfdbfec95f9c03c5c8c84c36ae2b2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1468,
    "chunk_text": "This is not the first time it happened. When Venezuela\u2019s President Nicolas Maduro was openly abducted after attacking the Capital of Venezuela, this Government said nothing about it. For all this, Venezuela is a country which follows Che Guevara and his principles and you all also started your organization on Che Guevara\u2019s principles. But, now, Sir, they have forgotten about Che Guevara, they have forgotten about Maduro and have totally ignored them. They have become so pally with the capitalist nations.\n\nIt is also regrettable, Sir, that many Gulf countries, including the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, have come under Iranian missile and drone attacks. It is regrettable. I have issued a statement to the press yesterday, where I have referred to that act, at least, in a summary way. I have said this, I quote:\n\n\"We also wish to express solidarity with the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, Qatar, Bahrain, Kuwait and Jordon, their peoples, and the broader region, as fear of wider regional conflict and global instability grows. We urge all parties to engage in constructive diplomacy.\n\nOur hope and prayer is for enduring peace and stability in the region, with meaningful de-escalation including nuclear disarmament and non-proliferation by Israel, while preserving the right of states to peaceful nuclear exploration and use. This should underpin a Greater Middle East built on mutual respect, cooperative security, and shared prosperity.\""
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-04-2026-03-04",
    "num": "2026-03-04",
    "date_str": "2026-03-04",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-03-04",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23360_english_2026-03-04.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-04-2026-03-04-0162",
    "chunk_index": 162,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "5c11f69ba8ca7e5e95d1e053376420e6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2051,
    "chunk_text": "Our hope and prayer is for enduring peace and stability in the region, with meaningful de-escalation including nuclear disarmament and non-proliferation by Israel, while preserving the right of states to peaceful nuclear exploration and use. This should underpin a Greater Middle East built on mutual respect, cooperative security, and shared prosperity.\"\n\n1689 1690\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nthe onslaught, have shown immense restraint during this holy month of Ramadan. Their maturity and pragmatic approach not to be drawn into the US-Israeli trap must be applauded. I must remind here what Henry Kissinger once said, I quote:\n\n\"To be an enemy of the U.S. is dangerous, but to be a friend is fatal.\"\n\nThat is what Kissinger said. I am sure these Middle East nations, though they are coming under attack by Iran, though it may be seen as provocative, are maintaining some resistance and are even willing to bear it for the sake of peace and refusing to join the US and Israel in this holy month of Ramadan. I must congratulate them for what they are doing.\n\nI must also quote here John F. Kennedy. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bb2\u0bc8\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd)\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Member, your time is over now.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dca \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd)\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Hon. Presiding Member, I will finish with what John F. Kennedy said, I quote:\n\n\"Those who foolishly sought power by riding the back of the tiger ended up inside.\"\n\nThat is what may happen, if this type of action is tolerated by anyone anywhere in this world."
  },
