    "chunk_text": "\u0bb5\u0bb4\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f \u0bb5\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bae\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bbf \u0baa\u0baf\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb2\u0bcd: \u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\n\n\u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bae\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0ba4\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc2\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1 PROACTIVE UTILIZATION OF OPPORTUNITIES PROVIDED BY COLOMBO SECURITY CONCLAVE: STATEMENT BY DEPUTY MINISTER OF DEFENCE\n\n1797 1798\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc2\u0dcf\u0dab\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dca \u0dcf\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dca,\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db1\u0dca \u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0 05\n\nSir, I wish to make a brief statement to this esteemed House on the engagement of Sri Lanka with the Colombo Security Conclave, outlining its background, evolution, current institutional arrangements, operational engagements and the present position of the Government with regard to the Secretariat and future cooperation.\n\nSir, the Colombo Security Conclave is a regional security cooperation framework among Indian Ocean littoral States originated in 2011 as a trilateral maritime security cooperation mechanism among Sri Lanka, India and the Maldives. The primary objective of this arrangement was to enhance maritime safety and security, information sharing and operational coordination in addressing common non-traditional security threats in the region.\n\nIn recognition of the evolving security environment and the increasing inter-linkages between maritime security, terrorism, cyber threats, transnational organized crime and disaster response, the mechanism was renamed and formalized as the Colombo Security Conclave in November, 2020. Over time, the scope of cooperation was expanded and structured around five agreed pillars, namely,\n\n\uf0b7 Maritime Safety and Security \uf0b7 Countering Terrorism and Radicalization \uf0b7 Combating Trafficking and Transnational Organised Crime \uf0b7 Cyber Security, Protection of Critical Infrastructure and Technology \uf0b7 Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief"
  },
