    "md5": "f4846adbe0236434ecec5f2e78800e5e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1444,
    "chunk_text": "\uf0b7 Maritime Safety and Security \uf0b7 Countering Terrorism and Radicalization \uf0b7 Combating Trafficking and Transnational Organised Crime \uf0b7 Cyber Security, Protection of Critical Infrastructure and Technology \uf0b7 Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief\n\nThe Colombo Security Conclave is a non-military alliance which functions on the principles of sovereign equality, mutual respect, consensus and non-interference, with a clear focus on addressing shared regional security challenges.\n\nSince its inception, the Colombo Security Conclave has convened six National Security Adviser-level meetings and eight Deputy National Security Adviser-level meetings, with hosting responsibilities rotating among member States. The decisions taken at the National Security Adviser-level are implemented through Joint Annual Action Plans prepared under each pillar and coordinated through the meetings of the National Lead Coordinators.\n\nIn institutional terms, it was decided that the Colombo Security Conclave Secretariat will be established in Colombo and accordingly, a Secretariat has been temporarily established at the Sri Lanka Navy Headquarters, and two officers of the Sri Lanka Navy are\n\npresently functioning at this Secretariat. Sri Lanka has also designated senior officers from relevant Ministries and agencies as pillar coordinators, who plan and conduct activities and awareness programmes with the participation of other member States."
