    "description": "Hansard of 2026-03-05",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23375_english_2026-03-05.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-05-2026-03-05-0051",
    "chunk_index": 51,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "3fe92c2d0cb944c696d8e48010fe670c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1925,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka has also participated in and contributed to a wide range of Colombo Security Conclave-related exercises, workshops, and training programmes. These activities are undertaken in accordance with the Joint Annual Action Plans agreed under the Colombo Security Conclave framework.\n\nIt is also pertinent to note that no separate national strategy has been formulated exclusively for the Colombo Security Conclave. Instead, Sri Lanka\u2019s engagement is guided by the jointly agreed Colombo Security Conclave\n\n1799 1800\n\n\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc0\n\nAction Plans, which cover counter-terrorism, cyber security, humanitarian assistance, disaster relief and other shared priorities.\n\nWith regard to governance arrangements, as agreed by member States, the first Secretary-General of the Colombo Security Conclave has been nominated by India. After that, the post of the Secretary-General will be rotated among member States in alphabetical order in accordance with the Memorandum of Understanding. There is no provision at present for a Deputy Secretary-General, though Sri Lanka has proposed the creation of such a post to be permanently held by a Sri Lankan during recent discussions in view of the Secretariat being established in Colombo. Each member State is, however, required to appoint a Director to assist the Secretary-General.\n\nOn matters relating to privileges, visas and facilities for foreign officials, no specific decisions have been taken pending the finalization of the Headquarters Agreement.\n\nSir, in conclusion, the engagement of Sri Lanka with the Colombo Security Conclave remains pragmatic, transparent and firmly aligned with national interests. The Government is committed to regional security cooperation while, at the same time, ensuring fiscal discipline, legal clarity and respect for national sovereignty as the Colombo Security Conclave continues to evolve. Thank you, Sir."
  },
