    "chunk_text": "8. Terminal -2 \u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddc \u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1 BIA\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dd3 \u0d82\u0dc4 \u0d85\u0db4\u0dc3\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca \u200d\u0dbb\u0ddc\u0db4\u0db0\u0dc1\u0dd3 \u0dc0\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dca \u0db4\u0dad\u0ddc\u0da7\u0dd4\u0db4 \u0ddc\u0dc5\u0dc0\u0d9a \u0d82\u0d9c\u0dc0\u0dca \u0dc3 \u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddc \u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1 \u0d87\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dc5\u0dd4\u0dc0 \u0d82\u0dd0\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0d9a\u0db1 \u0dbb \u0d87\u0dd2\u0db1 \u0db4\u0dc4\u0ddd \u0dca\u0daf\u0dd2 \u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dc3 \u0dc3\u0dc0 \u0dc0\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dca \u0db4\u0dad\u0ddc\u0da7\u0dd4\u0db4 \u0ddc\u0dc5 \u0d82\u0d9c\u0dc0\u0dca \u0dc3, \u0dca \u0dca\u0dad \u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddc \u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1 \u0d82\u0dc4 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dc3 \u0dcf \u0dc3\u0dad\u0dca\u0db4\u200d\u0dbb\u0dda\u0dab\u0dd2 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0db1 \u0db4\u0dab\u0ddc\u0dc3\u0dc0\u0ddc\u0daf? \u0d82\u0d9c\u0db1\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0dc0\u0dca \u0dc3 \u0dca\u0ddc \u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0dca\u0db3\u0dc0 \u0daf\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dca\u0dc3.\n\n1. A total of 29 scheduled airlines are operating from Sri Lanka, including two Sri Lankan carriers - the SriLankan Airlines and FitsAir. They have been\n\napproved to operate for the winter season 2025/2026. But, based on the approved aircraft capacities, the weekly one-way seat availability ranges from approximately 115,000 to 203,000 seats.\n\nHowever, given the prevailing situation in the Middle East, several airlines, namely Qatar Airways, Emirates, Air Arabia, Etihad Airways, Air Arabia Abu Dhabi, Flydubai, Kuwait Airways, Jazeera Airways, SriLankan Airlines and FitsAir, have either cancelled their scheduled flights or reduced their frequencies to and from Sri Lanka. Meanwhile, a few airlines such as Aeroflot, Edelweiss and SalamAir have introduced additional flights to meet the current demand from this region.\n\nFrom the second-half of this question, the Hon. Member asks about seating capacities and details of those airlines and their respective minimum and maximum seating capacities are given in Annex 01.\n\nAnnex 01\n\n2345 2346\n\n\u0ddc\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0db4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dc0\n\n2. a. Embarkation levy presently charged per passenger departing from airports in Sri Lanka.\n\nb. The above tax amount is included in the price of the air ticket\n\nc. It is transmitted to the Civil Aviation Authority accumulated by the airlines\n\nd. Twice a week\n\nUsually, this embarkation levy only applies to departures and is included in the price of the air ticket. The Civil Aviation Authority is responsible for collecting this tax, which is then transferred to the Treasury twice a week.\n\nName of the\n\nAirport\n\nDate of Issuing of\n\nTickets\n\nApplicable\n\nUSD Amount\n\na. Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) - (IATA code- CMB)\n\nFrom 01.02.2020 USD 60\n\nb. Jaffna International Airport (JIA) - (IATA code -JAF)\n\nFrom 01.02.2026 USD 60"
