  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-19-2026-03-19",
    "num": "2026-03-19",
    "date_str": "2026-03-19",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-03-19",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23381_english_2026-03-19.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-19-2026-03-19-0057",
    "chunk_index": 57,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "04a3efbaac5dead0b5926719ddfb7fe4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2006,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Minister, in your response, which I was eagerly listening to, there was one specific elimination. The President cited the Hingurakgoda Airport as a way forward and that has not been brought into the Answer. I presume it is part of this with its constructions ongoing.\n\nFurthermore, another most important aspect today is that, with the Middle East being in turmoil, also for the next month or so, we would have to bear the brunt of what is going on there. I would want you to really look at positioning Sri Lanka to take advantage of that situation, which I have been saying for the last 14 months. The Mattala Airport is a sleeping giant which could be awakened at this particular moment. There are two or three Qatar Airways flights which operate from here directly to Europe. Likewise, they also go to Muscat. So, use the Mattala Airport to our advantage. You could even offer free handling because the concomitant advantages we are going to get thereafter would be far greater. Hon. Minister, you have Qatar Airways which handles a seating capacity of roughly about 700,000 a week. Bring them in, speak to them and say, \u201cWe will give you free handling\u201d, and the rest would flow in thereafter. Likewise, with Etihad Airways and Emirates Airline, the same thing could be pursued.\n\nThe next one is cargo. Last time, I told the Hon. Minister of Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources that about 400 to 500 tons of fish perish due to lack of capacity. So, ensure that these all these areas are converted so that we could earn foreign exchange at this fairly decisive time. So, Hon. Minister, you have a big role to play with regard to both the Port and the Airport. You can bring them into Sri Lanka by sea and take them out by air. So, all these can be converted, if you adopt a forward-thinking approach.\n\nAll we could basically do is give you ideas and those must be crystalized soon because this type of situation would not last for the next two, three or four years. So, seize the opportunity."
  },
