  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-19-2026-03-19",
    "num": "2026-03-19",
    "date_str": "2026-03-19",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-03-19",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23381_english_2026-03-19.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-19-2026-03-19-0076",
    "chunk_index": 76,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "3d785bd65d9871bcfa0eecacfbe9212d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1143,
    "chunk_text": "At the same time, we are seeing is a strong requirement when we go through BoI inquiries. Now, with the new Investment Promotion Act, we are going to make it extremely clear what kind of investments are promoted in Sri Lanka and what kind of tax holidays each of those categories would get. If we take the extension of tax holidays, they could be extended up to ten years based on the investment. Those things had not been cleared over the past decade. That is why investments did not come to Sri Lanka.\n\nAlso, I am happy to say that this January, we have done extremely well compared to January, last year. The remittances have increased; our exports have increased and that is the trajectory we are on.\n\n2363 2364\n\n[\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca \u0db1\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0d85\u0db4\u0db6\u0dca\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0dc4 \u0dab\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc]\n\n2026 \u0dab\u0ddc\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4 19\n\nI also want to emphasize the national strategy on conserving energy. This is not a strategy to stop anything, but a strategy through which we are trying to preserve energy and see how far we could move without getting disrupted. To that strategy, every individual, every industry has to support and that is how things would go on."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-19-2026-03-19",
    "num": "2026-03-19",
    "date_str": "2026-03-19",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-03-19",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23381_english_2026-03-19.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-19-2026-03-19-0077",
    "chunk_index": 77,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "3f12cd7178998183509ceb5ac9e3af0d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2222,
    "chunk_text": "I also want to emphasize the national strategy on conserving energy. This is not a strategy to stop anything, but a strategy through which we are trying to preserve energy and see how far we could move without getting disrupted. To that strategy, every individual, every industry has to support and that is how things would go on.\n\nAt the same time, the Ministry of Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Co-operative Development, the Ministry of Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources, the Ministry of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation and also the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism are supporting all these industries. Those industries have a Line Ministry to reach out to and if there are those which are not registered under any Ministry, they can reach out to the Ministry of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development and we are there to support them.\n\nNow, our entire objective is to have a continuous fuel supply. We are very confident that with the intervention of the Minister of Energy, the Hon. President and the Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism, we could ensure a continuous supply of fuel and electricity. So, those are the two priorities of the country now. And, I hope the public will understand the situation and disregard the misinformation and false predictions that are being made by the Opposition continuously.\n\nThank you very much. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dca\u0db7\u0dcf \u0dca\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bc8\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees) \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0db1\u0dca\u0dab\u0ddc\u0dc3\u0ddc \u0dab\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dab\u0ddc. \u0d94\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dab\u0ddc\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc\u0da9\u0dd2 9 \u0ddc\u0d9a \u0dca \u0d9a\u0dd0\u0db4\u0dca\u0dc3\u0dc0\u0ddc.\n\n[\u0db4\u0dd6.\u0db7\u0ddc. 11.56] \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db4 \u0ddd\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0dba \u0ddc\u0dbb \u0d82\u0db7\u0ddc \u0d82\u0db7\u0ddc \u0dd2\u0db1\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd2 \u0db1\u0dd2, \u0db4\u0dab , \u0dbb\u0da7\u0da7, \u0db4\u0d9a\u0ddd \u0da7 \u200d\u0dbb\u0dc1\u0dda\u0dc3 \u0dca \u0dd2\u0db1\u0db4\u0dca\u0dc3 \u0d85\u0dc0\u0d82\u0dda\u0dcf\u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dca. \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dad\u0dca \u0dd6\u0db8\u0db4\u0db8\u0ddd\u0dd3\u0dba"
  },
