    "chunk_text": "withstand pain? \u201cIf we get pain, you also had better suffer it\u201d has been the attitude of the Iranians. And, the entire Third World is applauding them. If you take a popular vote or a public opinion in Sri Lanka today, every community will stand with Iran, not with the Americans or the Israelis; hardly anybody would. You can see that on social media.\n\nThat is the Convention the Hon. Vijitha Herath, Minister of Foreign Affairs spoke about at the famous panel discussion with Palki Sharma as moderator. I am not going to talk about the Hon. Minister of Foreign Affairs's language skills; that is not my intention. But, when the question was asked, he was giving a \"keheda yanne, malle pol\" answer. She was asking about that incident and Sri Lanka's response, but he was talking about the blue economy and UNCLOS all the time. What has the blue economy got to do with the question that was asked?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0db1\u0da5 \u0daf\u0dba\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dbb\u0dd2 \u0da2\u0dba\u0dc0\u0dca\u0db4\u0d9a\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0ba4\u0baf\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0bb1\u0bbf \u0b9c\u0baf\u0b9a\u0b9a\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb0) (The Hon. Dayasiri Jayasekara, Attorney-at-Law) The Green economy. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0db1\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0db4 \u0dc4\u0dc3\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) He was talking about the green economy, I am told.\n\nAnyway, whatever it is, the issue is, now, we have got our wires crossed in this entire conflict. We may have got some semblance of satisfaction in having rescued those sailors, but, ultimately, the goodwill with our friendly countries has been destroyed. That is what the Hon. Mujibur Rahman just pointed out, that at the Iftar ceremony yesterday, there was no one from the Muslim\n\nworld, except for Malaysia and Indonesia. Thank you very much for inviting us and we went there. Our President invited us. So, we should go. That is a different matter. But, what happened to the main countries in the Gulf Region? None of them came."
  },
