    "chunk_size_bytes": 1914,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dd2\u0db1 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0db1\u0da5 \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0db4\u0dca\u0db4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0bc8\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd. \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bbe\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. M. Nizam Kariapper, PC) Hon. Presiding Member, today, I rise with a deep sense of responsibility to address on the grave escalation of conflict unfolding in the Middle East.\n\nDid you not condemn it when President Nicolas Maduro was taken into custody by the US? Your Secretary did; the Minister of Foreign Affairs made a statement. They said it was \"interfering with an internal matter\". Sometimes, you all love to stand like deaf Members of Parliament, as if you have not heard what I am saying. It suited this Government to condemn the US's intervention in Venezuela and taking President Nicolas Maduro into custody when, in fact, the US and Donald Trump denied their involvement. But, on the 28th of February, 2026, Donald Trump went on to make the statement, \"We have eliminated a threat and now, it is time for the people of Iran to elect their own President\". That is a complete violation of the International Humanitarian Law - IHL. He made a fool out of himself, violating the International Humanitarian Law. Now, what is the problem in condemning that? Is it because Iran is a Muslim State? If you all had the guts to stand up against US intervention in Venezuela, you should have the guts to do the same when it happened to Iran. So, who brought pressure on you? That is my problem.\n\n2457 2458\n\n\u0ddc\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0db4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dc0\n\nThere is time till tomorrow. I am expecting the Hon. President to come here and answer my question. Why did he not condemn it? Why was not condolences expressed by the Government? That is the reason why we felt very bad about the attitude of this Government towards the attack on Iran."
  },
