    "chunk_size_bytes": 2179,
    "chunk_text": "\u0dc3\u0dad \u0dba\u0dba, \u0dc0\u0d9c\u0dd3\u0db8 \u0dc3\u0dad \u0dc3\u0d82\u0dd2\u0db3\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0dc3\u0dad\u0dad\u0dd2\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0db8 \u0dc3\u0db3\u0dad\u0dcf\n\n\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dda \u0db8\u0dd4\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0db8 \u0b89\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0bae\u0bae, \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc2\u0bb1\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0ba8\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bbf\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0bae\u0ba4\n\n\u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0ba4\u0b9a\u0baf\u0bcd\u0bc6\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb0\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bc1\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0bae\u0bc1\u0baf\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bbf\n\nGOVERNMENT\u2019S INITIATIVE ON ENSURING TRUTH,\n\nACCOUNTABILITY AND RECONCILIATION\n\nFurther, while previous Governments, at least, engaged in discussions on truth, reconciliation and accountability mechanisms, the present Government\u2019s policy framework focuses on governance and anti-corruption without clearly addressing war-time accountability and justice. Hon. Minister of Justice, the mandate you got was not only to deal with corruption, but also to address accountability and justice issues.\n\n1. What is the Government\u2019s current official estimate of persons missing during the final stages of the armed conflict in 2009 and has that been updated?\n\n2. Does the Government accept that there is still no credible consolidated database of missing persons and what steps are being taken to establish one?\n\n3. What is the status of investigations into the Chemmani mass graves discovered in 2025 and the timeline for forensic analysis, identification and accountability?\n\n4. How many mass grave sites have been officially identified to date and what progress has been made in those investigations?\n\n5. Will the Government permit or seek international forensic and investigative assistance into these cases?\n\n6. What is the Government\u2019s position on individuals who allegedly surrendered to the military in the final days of the war and are now missing?\n\n7. Will the Government utilize evidence compiled by the Sri Lanka Accountability Project - SLAP - in pursuing such cases?\n\n8. What outcomes has the Office on Missing Persons delivered since this Government assumed office?\n\n9. What actions has the Office for Reparations taken and how does the Government respond to concerns that reparations without truth and justice are insufficient?\n\n2521 2522\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dad\u0dd4 20"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-20-2026-03-20",
    "num": "2026-03-20",
    "date_str": "2026-03-20",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-03-20",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23396_english_2026-03-20.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-20-2026-03-20-0053",
    "chunk_index": 53,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "1214799d8ce8117d21734b3cdde6ef75",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1687,
    "chunk_text": "8. What outcomes has the Office on Missing Persons delivered since this Government assumed office?\n\n9. What actions has the Office for Reparations taken and how does the Government respond to concerns that reparations without truth and justice are insufficient?\n\n2521 2522\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dad\u0dd4 20\n\nHon. Minister, I am asking you these questions in light of your President having been in power for a year and six months now and most of these concerns have still not been addressed. I have asked the Hon. Prime Minister two such questions previously under Questions posed to Hon. Prime Minister, and she also confirmed that it is work in progress. But, we are yet to see any concrete steps; as Representatives of the victim community, we are unable to see them.\n\nEspecially, with regard to the Chemmani mass graves - you have unearthed a certain number of skeletons - there has been no forensic analysis or anything; you have not done anything. Unearthing further skeletons is another matter, but with regard to the skeletons or the remains found so far, what have you all done?\n\nAnd, one last matter I would like to add, Hon. Minister, is the issue of political prisoners. The previous Government under President Ranil Wickremesinghe used to engage with us and even though we did not accept the TRC, they, at least, had a proposal. When we demanded the release of political prisoners, they released, at least, one or two. Actually, President Ranil Wickremesinghe released a few. But, you all have not released any. You are not even agreeing that there are political prisoners.\n\nSo, in light of this situation, Hon. Minister, I would like to have answers to my Question.\n\nThank you."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-20-2026-03-20",
