    "md5": "1a79777f2a540a17416926608b18c91c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1298,
    "chunk_text": "The Office on Missing Persons has reported information relating to 19 mass grave sites and it is currently working closely with eight sites located in Colombo, Mullaitivu, Mannar, Batticaloa and Trincomalee. Overall, the OMP plays a critical role in advancing its mandate by expanding its operations. For this, technical support was obtained from the ICRC through workshops on forensic archaeology and engaging in training more than 40 excavation officers from the Department of Archaeology, who were trained on mass grave investigations. An extension of the workshop on advanced forensic archaeology was also organized with 60 participants from the Department of Archaeology. This training and technical support was provided to the expert team in order to create a pool of Excavation Officers to investigate the mass graves and to accelerate the process in finding out the fate of the missing persons. The OMP is working closely with the ICRC and there are commitments established to work collaboratively for the next three years. So, we are working with them.\n\nto repeat. However, we have to accept the fact that during a period of war, people are made to disappear by both sides. It is not right, but wrong, and we stand against it. But, that is the nature of war. However, we do not justify it."
