    "md5": "c7f407e2c1c2c5e09d9a3eaf7902d6bd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 942,
    "chunk_text": "Also, if I add a few things - this will be officially communicated in time to come - how they have unilaterally gathered facts and the methodologies used are something that we cannot accept, and we have maintained it to be that way.\n\n8. Since assuming office, the Government has supported and strengthened the work of the Office on Missing Persons - OMP- resulting in several tangible outcomes:\n\n2525 2526\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dc2\u0dba \u0db1\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4 \u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dad\u0dd4 20\n\nrecruited nearly 100 people to carry out the work of the OMP and the OR. And, they were extremely short of staff and was not functional. Now, we have also allocated them money. So, now what has happened? Cabinet Approval has been granted to extend the OMP\u2019s mandate to inquire cases beyond the year 2000 and newly reported cases, too. So, now, there are more cases being reported and the numbers are going up."
  },
  {
