    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka has long approached global affairs with prudence, balance and moral clarity. We were a principled voice within the Non-Aligned Movement and not passive observers, but advocates of independent justice. To this day, we still maintain that stand. Non-alignment was never indifference; it gave the courage to uphold principle without becoming entangled in great power rivalries. Today, as global polarization deepens, once again that principle remains not only relevant, but necessary.\n\nvessel returning from the same exercise was granted access to a Sri Lankan port, where necessary steps were taken to ensure the safety of the vessel and well-being of its cadets. In doing so, Sri Lanka demonstrated that responsible conduct in international waters is an obligation, not a choice.\n\nSir, the oceans that connect our nations must never become spaces where humanity is forgotten. Ships may carry different flags, their crews may come from different lands, but distress at sea is universal. So, too, must be our response. Sri Lanka\u2019s actions reflect principles that remain fundamental to a stable international order.\n\nSri Lanka, though modest in size, has consistently shown that principled action carries influence. Situated at the crossroads of civilizations, we have every reason to advocate dialogue over division and cooperation over conflict.\n\nThe Indian Ocean carries the aspirations of nearly half the world\u2019s population. It must remain a region of stability, not rivalry. The vision of a \u201cZone of Peace\u201d is not a relic of the past, but it is a necessity for the future and the present."
