    "chunk_text": "The Indian Ocean carries the aspirations of nearly half the world\u2019s population. It must remain a region of stability, not rivalry. The vision of a \u201cZone of Peace\u201d is not a relic of the past, but it is a necessity for the future and the present.\n\nSir, whilst I stand on the Floor of this August House, I wish to address a matter of paramount importance which the world can no longer afford to treat with cautionary silence. At this very moment in history, humanity has placed in the hands of a very few individuals the authority to command armed forces and in some cases, to unleash weapons capable of irreversible and catastrophic destruction. The consequences of a single misjudgement, a moment of emotional disability or instability or a failure of restraint are no longer confined within borders. They are global, immediate and permanent and most often, irreversible for a very long time. Therefore, on behalf of the peace-loving citizens everywhere, I make a sincere, yet urgent appeal to the parliaments, congresses and peoples\u2019 assemblies of the world that the time has come to move beyond convention and institutionalize stronger safeguards around the exercise of such extraordinary power. It is both reasonable and responsible for nations to ensure that those entrusted with command authority are subject to rigorous, independent and internationally benchmarked assessments of their mental and emotional fitness conduced with dignity, transparency and at regular intervals during their tenure. This is not an affront to leadership, but it is a reinforcement of trust.\n\n2575 2576\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0"
