    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, we meet today at a serious moment in the life of our nation. Sri Lanka had recently passed through bankruptcy and even today, we are still in the process of rebuilding our economy, restoring stability and regaining the confidence of our people as well as of the international community. When this Government assumed office under the leadership of the Hon. President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, we did not inherit a stable country. We inherited a country burdened by debt, weakened by years of financial indiscipline and shaken by loss of public trust. Public trust is the most important thing. People were not asking for promises; they were asking for stability. The responsibility before the National People\u2019s Power Government was, therefore, clear. It was not to proceed recklessly and to make popular announcements, but to stabilize the nation. We were very successful in that. We had to restore discipline in public finance, rebuild confidence in the financial system, ensure that fuel, electricity, LP gas, medicine and all other essential goods are available and to regain confidence of international institutions and friendly nations. So, these were not easy decisions, but necessary decisions.\n\n2581 2582\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0daf\u0dba\u0dcf\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dd2\u0dba \u0dba\u0dba\u0d9c\u0dc3\u0dda\u0d9a\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4 \u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dad\u0dd4 20\n\nSir, today, the world itself is passing through a period of serious uncertainty. The conflict in the Middle East is not a distant event for Sri Lanka. Energy prices have been affected; shipping routes have been affected; air travel has been affected and tourism is also affected. Global markets have became unstable than ever before. Most importantly, thousands of Sri Lankans working overseas have been directly affected. Foreign employment is one of the strongest pillars of our economy. Remittances from our migrant workers have helped this country survive during the most difficult times."
