    "chunk_index": 151,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "571870c723722aaeec0947887e1ea53c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2017,
    "chunk_text": "As a country located near major energy and shipping routes, any instability in those waters could directly affect our fuel supply, trade and economic stability. For that reason, Sri Lanka supports the freedom of navigation, the security of maritime transport and peaceful use of oceans in accordance with the international laws. For small nations, these rules are not theoretical, but are essential for their survival.\n\nSir, in this challenging global environment, we must not only face challenges, but also explore opportunities. Sri Lanka\u2019s location, its ports, airports and maritime position would give us advantage, if they are used wisely. We are working to strengthen tourism, aviation, maritime transport, logistics and energy security. In the past, some opportunities were lost due to poor planning, but, today, the approach is different. We plan carefully, act responsibly and protect national assets. Sir, the duty of a responsible government is to protect the country and the duty of a responsible opposition is not to weaken the country during time of crisis. Democracy allows criticism, but it also requires responsibility.\n\nSir, we love this country. Because we love this country, we cannot allow it to fall into instability, have divisions or suffer due to irresponsible decisions again. Patriotism is not shown by speaking as loudest as possible, but by protecting the nation when it is still under pressure and by putting Sri Lanka before politics.\n\nSir, if we remain disciplined and united and if we continue on the path of responsibility, Sri Lanka would overcome every challenge before it, and this Government will take all necessary measures to ensure that the country is stable and strong.\n\nThank you very much. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bc6\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) The next speaker is the Hon. R.M. Ranjith Madduma Bandara. You have nine minutes."
  },
